From b1736517ae9f56b7ef37e453f48c177b2b96d6cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ETenal <etenal@etenal.me>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 07:36:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add tracefs object watcher scripts and profiles

This commit introduces a new set of scripts for tracing object lifecycles using tracefs. The main script, `tracefs-object-watch.sh`, provides a command-line interface for starting, stopping, and running tracing sessions with various profiles.

Additionally, it includes:
- A library file `lib.sh` with utility functions for managing trace events.
- Profiles for cache-backed objects and request sockets, allowing users to monitor specific events related to memory allocation and deallocation.
- A control header file `poc_control.h` for sending commands to the tracing process.

These additions enhance the tracing capabilities of the kernel, enabling more detailed monitoring of object lifecycles in memory management.

Signed-off-by: [Your Name] <your.email@example.com>
