Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add README for tracefs object watcher framework

This commit introduces a comprehensive README file for the tracefs object watcher framework, detailing its purpose, directory layout, high-level design, and usage instructions. The document outlines the framework's capabilities for tracing object lifecycles and specific events, as well as providing guidance on adding new object watchers and integrating with proof-of-concept applications.

Key sections include:
- Overview of the framework's functionality and intended use cases.
- Description of the core runner and profile structure.
- Instructions for common commands and wrapper mode semantics.
- Guidelines for extending the framework and adding new profiles.

This documentation enhances user understanding and facilitates effective utilization of the tracing capabilities.

Signed-off-by: [Your Name] <your.email@example.com>
---
